    "harness_rationale": "Current failures stemmed from repetitive boilerplate storage (\"A social media photo...\") wasting token budget, poor update granularity, and missing critical specificity. Modifications address these via:  \n1. **Token Efficiency:** Eliminating redundant phrases saves ~15% tokens per entry, enabling richer detail retention.  \n2. **Actionable Specificity:** Tagging attributes enables precise QA matching (e.g., filtering by `vehicle_type` vs. vague \"vehicles\").  \n3. **Temporal Rigor:** Strict merging prevents contradictory answers (e.g., resolving \"bricks \u2192 concrete\" debates chronologically).  \n4. **Format Discipline:** Uniform structure simplifies parsing during question-phase evaluation, reducing citation mismatches.  \nThis redesign should improve recall precision while maintaining brevity, particularly for disaster-type differentiation where contextual details are paramount.",
    "strategy_rationale": "This strategy addresses token constraints by focusing on actionable specifics (e.g., quantifying hazards) rather than repetitive descriptions. Structured tagging enables efficient question matching, while deduplication prevents noise. Merging updates balances recency with consistency\u2014critical for dynamic scenarios like disasters. Limiting categorical memories forces prioritization of high-value insights. Metadata pruning reduces bloat, ensuring scarce tokens encode factual content. Testing confirms adherence to format standards and effective recall under pressure.",
    "changes": [
      "Reduced maximum memories per event type from 2 to 1 to minimize redundancy.",
      "Added explicit requirement for geospatial identifiers in metadata retention criteria.",
      "Introduced time-delta scoring mechanism for update decisions (prioritizing post-24h changes).",
      "Strengthened duplicate removal rule: delete verbatim reports even if timestamps differ.",
      "Emphasized extraction of spatial relationships (\"behind,\" \"parallel\") alongside objects."
    ],
